SOURCE CODE
Source code and releases: https://github.com/flynnsbit/misterplex-cast
(releases: https://github.com/flynnsbit/misterplex-cast/releases). The source for the MiSTerPlex program, the boot
scripts, the cast helpers and the packaging scripts is there and is also
available under the written offer below.
The complete corresponding source is this repository, https://github.com/flynnsbit/misterplex-cast.
The on-card AirPlay helper is built from FFmpeg 8.1.2, x264, and OpenSSL 3.0.15.
This repository ships that helper's licence text and checksums
(packaging/licenses/gcast-ffmpeg/NOTICE), not the helper source tarballs.
Written offer: for three years from the date of a release that contains these
programs, the distributor will provide the corresponding source on a physical
medium for no more than the cost of distribution.
https://github.com/flynnsbit/misterplex-cast/issues

FORKED AND VENDORED CODE
For the changes to forked code, see this repository.
- PlexOB core: a modified fork of the MiSTer_h264_decoder project by owenb321
  (upstream's licence is GPL-3.0-or-later). The RTL file headers keep the upstream
  notices unchanged. Upstream credit: owenb321,
  https://github.com/owenb321/MiSTer_h264_decoder . The PlexOB core and the
  MiSTerPlex daemons are GPL-3.0-or-later. Upstream's h264/ files carry no
  per-file licence header; the grant is upstream's NOTICE (fpga/owenb-combo-s9/PlexOB_480p/vendor-upstream/NOTICE).
- MIT exception: owenb's vendored hps/ directory (the HPS client library from
  MiSTer_h264_decoder) stays MIT. In this repo that tree is
  third_party/owenb-h264ring (its LICENSE is upstream hps/LICENSE). In the
  export the same files sit at
  fpga/owenb-combo-s9/PlexOB_480p/vendor-upstream/hps/ with hps/LICENSE beside
  them. That MIT grant does not cover the FPGA core or the daemons.
- This package ships one FPGA core, MiSTerPlex.rbf (built from the PlexOB
  core; older builds named it PlexOB.rbf). It does not ship Plex.rbf.
- Altera/Intel: the FPGA tree contains the MiSTer framework (Template_MiSTer,
  MiSTer-devel) sys/ files and other files that carry Altera Corporation / Intel
  Corporation copyright and licence notices. Those notices are kept unchanged in the
  tarball (in the file headers and in upstream's NOTICE) and apply to those files.
- Licence texts are in packaging/licenses/. Note: packaging/licenses/rbf/GPL-2 is the
  GPL-2 text and packaging/licenses/rbf/LICENSE is the GPL-3 text (same as LICENSE).
  See packaging/licenses/rbf/README.md. x264's GPL-2.0-or-later text is
  packaging/licenses/x264/COPYING. Forked RTL grant: fpga/NOTICE.

BUNDLED THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS (each keeps its own licence; texts and versions
are in packaging/licenses/)
- UxPlay (FDH2): AirPlay receiver library. LGPL-2.1-or-later, parts GPL-3.0.
- RPiPlay (FD-) crypto code and playfair (via UxPlay): GPL-3.0-or-later / GPL-3.0.
- csrp (Tom Cocagne), llhttp: MIT.  mdnsd (via UxPlay): LGPL-2.1-or-later.
- libplist (libimobiledevice): LGPL-2.1-or-later.
- FFmpeg 8.1.2: libav linked into misterplexd is LGPL-2.1-or-later. The
  on-card helper ffmpeg is configured --enable-gpl --enable-version3
  --enable-libx264 --enable-openssl, so the helper binary is distributed under GPL version 3; ffprobe
  has no libx264 or --enable-gpl and is LGPL-2.1-or-later with OpenSSL.
- x264 (VideoLAN): in the helper ffmpeg only. GPL-2.0-or-later
  (packaging/licenses/x264/COPYING).
- OpenSSL 3.0.15: Apache-2.0 (static in the helper ffmpeg and ffprobe).
- yt-dlp 2026.08.19 armv7l PyInstaller build: Unlicense. It packs a CPython
  runtime (PSF License) and the PyInstaller bootloader (GPL-2.0 with the
  bootloader exception). update_ytdlp.sh checks a network download against
  upstream SHA2-256SUMS from the same GitHub origin (corruption only; not a
  signature). Optional pins, default off: YTDLP_PIN_VERSION (release tag
  instead of latest) and YTDLP_PIN_SHA256 (exact 64-hex of the zip). Set both.
  A SHA pin alone still follows latest.
- stb (Sean Barrett): public domain.  QOI (Dominic Szablewski): MIT.
- Roboto (Google): Apache-2.0 (host/libmisterplex/plexui/third_party).
- Spleen 8x16 2.2.0 (Frederic Cambus): BSD-2-Clause (THIRD_PARTY.md).
- Mozilla CA bundle (curl.se extract): MPL-2.0.
- curl and the GNU C Library / GCC runtime come with the MiSTer's own Linux:
  curl licence (MIT-style); glibc LGPL-2.1-or-later; GCC GPL-3.0 with the
  runtime exception.

